Z||000000||85ZainoGT||09-28-2001||01:05 PM||||Im not sure which one I would prefer...  I like manuals, they are funner, but if your with a girl you want an auto, or if you have a turbo, id want an auto... whats your opinions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||kempo||09-28-2001||01:30 PM||||Manual tranny is the only way to go.  I am not sure why you'd want an automatic if you're with the ladies, perhaps you could enlighten me?  As far as turbos and superchargers go, the only way to have it would be a Stick Shift.  With an automatic, the car drives you, with a standard, you drive the car.  It all comes down to personal prefrences.  The standard fiero's are so much peppier than the automatic ones.  I don't mind automatic if it's a minivan or a pickup truck or whathaveyou, but a stick is the only way to go!  Peace!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||09-28-2001||01:49 PM||||Funner? The correct, incorrect word is "more gooder"!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> For me it depends on the car. On my stock 88 GT I love shifting through the gears and hearing the great exhaust sounds. On my friends 4.9 swap we are going with the 4-speed auto. When you have that much torque who cares. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Rick 88||||reg||12
Z||000003||Voytek||09-28-2001||01:56 PM||||Got one of each and like the change every 6 months.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-28-2001||02:01 PM||||Got one of each.  Stuck in traffic-automatic||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||09-28-2001||02:06 PM||||My 88 Formula = Automatic<BR>dad's 85 SE 2m6 = 4-spd Manual<P>I really like taking the 4-spd out to drive around in.  Tons of fun and a little faster off the line than my Formula!<P>For daily driving (read: rush hour commuter traffic and very crowded roads) I prefer the auto.  Especially with the Fiero clutch having to be burried into the carpet every time!  <P>The Auto is fun to drive too.  Its also nice to just mash the go pedal and go.<P>That clutch and shifting business just gets in the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  j/k!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero5||09-28-2001||02:16 PM||||Our fleet includes pretty much an equal selection of both autos and standards. I personally prefer a standard. I love driving Fiero5 with the 5 speed, but I have to say the 4 speed in my Fiero1 is incredible! Thanks Dad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I like the fact that with a standard, I can shift when I want. This allows me to speed up much quicker off the line.<BR>I would love to slap a 5 speed in my Fiero9. That would be awesome! Anyone need a good automatic tranny?<BR>I also like the standard when you have car trouble, as you can do more to get it going like popping the clutch.<BR>I find the auto's are good for daily driving in heavy traffic, or for those just learning to drive. It's again all personal preference though and what driving style you prefer.<P>I love shifting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Especially as I blow away those ricer mobiles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000007||LarryB||09-28-2001||02:36 PM||||All it takes is a few trips from the Massachusetts Turnpike up I-95 to I-93 on a Friday afternoon to appreciate an automatic. ||||reg||1
