Z||000034||Gerald||09-30-2001||05:21 PM||||5 spd, thats all I got ta say about that||||reg||1
Z||000035||pontiacs4me||09-30-2001||05:52 PM||||I hear more times on this forum about how many clutches get burned up, and this and that about manuals going bad, I go auto.  I know its slower in a stock v6 fiero, but when you start making power the only way to go is auto.  it takes a half a second to shift, if you are good at shifting.  but with an auto as fast as you can snap your fingers, it shifted.  I raced a guy in a 5.0 mustang in my firebird a while back.  He had a 5 speed and was a good driver, our cars were very well matched, but I noticed every time he shifted I picked up a quarter of a car legnth on him.  And when my auto shifted the car actually jumped foward a half a car.<BR>and I guess it could also be what engine your running.  There endless debate about this issue, im just stating my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000036||roadwarrior||09-30-2001||06:04 PM||||no matter how much power you make stick is the way to go, but when you make serious power go with a slap(rachet) shifter or a semi auto, I'm working on plans for a ratchet shift for my twin turbo 2.5||||reg||1
